# Public client identifiers for the production build.
#
# None of these are secrets: they are compiled into the JavaScript bundle and
# already served publicly at joshcocciardi.com. The same Firebase config is
# committed in apps/playball/js/store.js and apps/canitwo/js/store.js.
# Access control lives in firestore.rules and in the OAuth client's list of
# authorized origins — not in the secrecy of these values.
#
# They are committed so CI can reproduce the production build. For local
# development, copy .env.example to .env instead.

